---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = "/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-drip";
const title = "Yotpo Email & SMS to Drip: Shopify migration decisions";
const desc = "Evaluate Drip around explicit Shopify workflow rules, with a separate plan for retained Yotpo Reviews, Loyalty and any SMS program.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does Drip replace all Yotpo products?",
    "answer": "Moving email does not replace review display, review collection or a points program. Retain or replace those independently, and verify any data route needed for Drip messages."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should a Drip rehearsal cover?",
    "answer": "Inspect Shopify data, a wholesale exclusion, a gift purchaser and a repeat purchase that should exit replenishment. Prepare these as evaluation exercises; this page reports no observed outcomes."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p></header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>The comparison has become a migration decision</h2>
      <p>Yotpo Email & SMS is retired. Its live lifecycle notice says the dashboard and associated background services are inactive. Keeping Yotpo Reviews or Loyalty does not restore messaging. Evaluate a replacement sender while treating those retained products as separate services; the old suite-versus-standalone recommendation no longer describes an available choice.</p>
      <h2>Connect store data before designing branches</h2>
      <p>Drip documents syncing Shopify customers, orders and products, with an app embed for page and product-view tracking. Wait for the initial sync before judging missing product blocks. Installing the connection alone does not start automated emails. In a proposed rehearsal, inspect a repeat buyer and a recent order before creating workflow conditions; a visible canvas cannot compensate for missing source data.</p>
      <h2>Make wholesale and gift-buyer exclusions explicit</h2>
      <p>The useful reason to evaluate Drip is the work your operator needs to express and maintain. For a mixed retail/wholesale store, define which reliable field identifies trade buyers and where it enters Drip. Draft a retail welcome path with a wholesale exclusion, then change that field on a sample record and inspect the resulting eligibility. Gift purchasers may need seasonal reminders rather than a replenishment series aimed at the recipient. Do not infer either distinction from order value alone.</p>
      <h2>Replenishment needs a business rule before a delay</h2>
      <p>For consumables, write down whether timing follows the purchased item, a bundle or a subscription renewal. Rehearse another purchase before the scheduled reminder and a refund after workflow entry. Check which documented events and fields support those exits. If a proposed product attribute is unavailable, simplify the rule or budget a maintained data route rather than claiming arbitrary SKU-level automation is automatic.</p>
      <h2>Keep Reviews and Loyalty without inventing a connector</h2>
      <p>Retaining Yotpo review collection and on-site display is a separate decision from moving email to Drip. Name the review-request sender and leave that request out of Drip unless a supported integration and its configuration are established. For points-based email, verify the actual event or property route, customer matching and update behavior before drafting a balance claim. This page does not establish a native Drip connection for every Yotpo module.</p>
      <h2>Account for channels and maintenance</h2>
      <p>Scope Drip as the email candidate in this evaluation; establish the destination and transfer requirements for any SMS program separately. Include integration upkeep, template rebuilding and operator time in the budget. Keep a record of the customer fields used in each branch so another marketer can safely change a promotion. There is no supported contact-count price estimate or fixed trial duration in this comparison.</p>
      <h2>Reconstruct the program from accessible records</h2>
      <p>Start with prior exports, saved templates, consent evidence, suppression records and Shopify data you can legitimately access. Do not promise a fresh export from the retired Yotpo dashboard. Ask support what recovery remains possible before setting a launch date. A customer email or phone number in an order record does not establish marketing permission. Preserve opt-outs and mark unknown consent for review rather than importing every customer as subscribed.</p>
      <h2>Activate against a message ownership map</h2>
      <p>List welcome, cart, checkout recovery, post-purchase education, review collection, loyalty notices and winback separately. Prepare replacement messages disabled and inspect purchase exits, opt-outs and missing fields before activation. Give each trigger one live owner, including Shopify automations and retained Yotpo modules. Record who can pause each sender if a customer receives the wrong sequence. These are proposed acceptance exercises, not tests we ran or evidence of revenue lift.</p>
      <h2>Primary sources</h2>
      <p>Product information checked November 25, 2026. <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo lifecycle notice</a> · <a class="link" href="https://help.drip.com/hc/en-us/articles/4424695491725-Connect-Your-Shopify-Store">Drip Shopify setup</a></p>
    </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-drip">Omnisend vs Drip</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend">Yotpo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/food-and-beverage">Email apps for food & beverage</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/subscription-boxes">Email apps for subscription boxes</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Migration questions" />
</BaseLayout>
